# Swim water, surface row (TileKind::Swim, D-076): the Wolfgangsee as
# "Badewasser" - calm and clear, clearly unlike the lethal
# tile_wolfgangsee_water. A flat s surface skin (no wave crests, no
# transparent top) with a w glint drifting right and a short s streak
# drifting left, a t band, then clear t water with a sparse s caustic net
# that deepens into T with t caustics at the bottom (same net as
# tile_see_wasser_tief, so the lines run on across the tile edge). No
# dither, no dark b/B bands. The caustic net shimmers (its cell points
# circle by 1 px over the 4 frames).
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grids are the source.
sprite = tile_see_wasser
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = idle frames=4 ticks=12 loop
